; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR LIFE RACE  -  VM2: native 1802 via RUNMC   (loads at $5000)   (web copy based at $4000: the Multitasking page moves program 2 to $5000 itself)
; ==========================================================================
; Load BOTH programs - Life-Race-VM1.lst at $4000 and Life-Race-VM2.lst at
; $5000 - then cold-boot. The same Game of Life board (a 24 x 10 acorn) runs on
; both sides: VM1 on the left computes each generation in STELLAR bytecode, VM2
; on the right in native 1802 through $F1 RUNMC. After 8 generations VM1 copies
; VM2's count out of VM2's R1 ($D3), stops VM2 with $CF KILLVM, prints the score.
;
; Every board row is ONE PRINTSTR of a ready-made "ESC[rr;ccH" + 24 cells string,
; so the two VMs never garble each other's output. VT100 cursor addressing only.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/liferace_verify.py, V0061.33, two-VM cold boot): all 1,084 boards drawn (VM1 generations 0-8, VM2 0-1074) match a Python Life model; VM2 did 1075 generations to VM1's 8 - about 134 times as many. The scheduler switches on an opcode COUNT, so the Elf2K should print the same score. Run time: ~65.8 million 1802 instructions (~6.5 min at 3 MHz) plus ~372 KB of output (~6.5 min at 9600 baud): expect about 13 minutes.
; NOT YET RUN ON HARDWARE.
;
; 120 STELLAR commands.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 5000 CD             START
; D 5001 D0 12          SHAREVM on, read/write             VM1 reads our GEN word - and KILLVM needs RW
; D 5003 11 01 00 00    LOADXI R1 0000
; WAIT:
; D 5007 D3 10 B4       COPYVXY VM1 RB -> R4               VM1's GO register
; D 500A 86 04 00 01    TESTXI R4 0001
; D 500E A1 00 07       IFFALSEI WAIT                      Wait for VM1 to clear the screen
; D 5011 23 00 17       COPYXY R1 -> R7
; D 5014 11 0E 00 00    LOADXI R14 0000
; D 5018 11 08 03 E8    LOADXI R8 03E8
; D 501C 4D 78          DIVXY R7 / R8
